# Control Panel Development

**Project Type:** Vacation Work / Engineering Project
**Role:** Engineering Student / Project Contributor
**Focus:** Electrical Control, Panel Assembly and Wiring

## Project Overview

During my vacation work, I was involved in the **construction and assembly of an electrical control panel**. The project provided practical experience in translating an electrical control design into a functional physical system.

My work involved assembling the control panel, installing and organising electrical components, carrying out panel wiring, and ensuring that connections were made correctly and safely. The project also strengthened my understanding of practical electrical systems and how individual components are integrated into a complete control system.

## Engineering Skills Developed

* Electrical control panel assembly
* Electrical wiring and component integration
* Reading and interpreting electrical connections
* Practical fault identification and troubleshooting
* Understanding of control-system architecture
* Safe and organised electrical work practices
* Applying engineering knowledge in a practical working environment

## Project Outcome

The experience allowed me to develop practical engineering skills beyond academic coursework and gain a better understanding of how electrical control systems are constructed and implemented in an industrial environment.

